 "overview": "The Medford Board of Health is responsible for managing local public health policies, enforcing housing and environmental health codes, overseeing food and biosafety permitting, and directing municipal prevention programs. The archive documents 16 meetings of the board spanning from October 18, 2022, to October 13, 2026. Across this period, the board has updated tobacco regulations, allocated opioid settlement funding, managed housing code violations, and expanded mobile health and immunization services. As of the October 13, 2026 meeting, the board approved a food manufacturing grease trap variance, reviewed a Biosafety Level 2 permit application for 200 Boston Avenue, discussed aligning tobacco permit suspension rules with state law, and received a quarterly infectious disease report.",
 "threads": [
  {
   "name": "Tobacco and nicotine regulation",
   "status": "ongoing",
   "summary": "The board updated local tobacco regulations in early 2023 to establish business suspensions for sales to minors. It later discussed a Tobacco-Free Generation initiative to restrict nicotine sales by birth date, ultimately tabling the measure to monitor regional and state developments. In 2026, the board maintained a May 1 enforcement deadline for products lacking FDA marketing granted orders and approved suspension guidelines for second-offense violations. At its October 2026 meeting, the board considered aligning local suspension rules with state language.",
